# TransitHike

> Weekend day hikes you can reach by train from the city, with a train back the same evening. Free, with no account.

TransitHike finds mapped hiking routes (OpenStreetMap) near commuter, regional, and intercity train stations, leaving
out places the subway reaches. It only lists hikes with a trip back the same evening that leaves time to hike all of
each by sunset, at about 2 miles an hour with breaks. Each hike has its trains there and back, the last trip back,
the sunset, its length
(loop, out and back, or one way to transit home), how far it climbs, photos of nature along it, and timetables.
Transit times come from Transitous, so check them before you go.

